GreenX
https://github.com/nomad-coe/greenX
Licensed under the Apache License, Version 2.0.

  * src/Base/utils/minimax_omega_data.json
  * src/Base/utils/minimax_tau_data.json
    Minimax quadrature grid tables derived from the GreenX library, loaded
    by src/Base/utils/grids.py.

  * src/Base/utils/grids.py
    The table lookup follows GreenX's GX-TimeFrequency/src/minimax_utils.F90:
    the energy-range column selection of find_erange and the narrow-range
    stretch of coeffs_and_weights, applied with the sign each axis carries
    (minimax_omega.F90 divides, minimax_tau.F90 multiplies). Modifications:
    written as one shared helper serving both axes, and the grids are returned
    in atomic units rather than accumulated into a quadrature in place.

  * src/Base/utils/time_frequency.py
    Python port of the imaginary time <-> imaginary frequency transformation
    weights from GreenX's GX-TimeFrequency/src/minimax_grids.F90, namely the
    routines get_transformation_weights and calculate_psi_and_mat_A, together
    with the transformation-type codes of minimax_utils.F90. Modifications:
    reorganized as a single grid object carrying both axes and all four
    transform matrices; Tikhonov regularization applied automatically above
    20 points; a finite-temperature (IR) backend added behind the same
    interface, which is not GreenX-derived. The per-point regularized
    least-squares fit and its target function follow the original.
